The complexity and diversity of sports movements pose great challenges to recognition algorithms. Based on GCN, a motion pose estimation model is first designed. Then, based on this, a dynamic ST-GCN AR model is constructed.
The estimation of human body posture is the foundation of AR. By accurately estimating the key points of the human body, key information can be provided for AR, helping models understand sports movements [15, 16]. In this regard, the study first conducts action posture estimation based on GCN. GCN is a deep learning model that has been specifically designed for processing graph-structured data. GCN comprises two main domains: the spectral domain and the spatial domain. The research adopts the spatial domain-based GCN for attitude estimation. The input of GCN is the node feature matrix in the graph data and the adjacency matrix of the graph. The node feature matrix contains the initial feature representation of each node, and the adjacency matrix describes the connection relationship between nodes [17, 18]. The graph data are defined as\documentclass[12pt]{minimal} \usepackage{amsmath} \usepackage{wasysym} \usepackage{amsfonts} \usepackage{amssymb} \usepackage{amsbsy} \usepackage{mathrsfs} \usepackage{upgreek} \setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt} \begin{document}$$\wp =\left(V,E\right)$$\end{document}, where V and E refer to "nodes" and "edges" respectively, corresponding to the connection relationship between human keypoints and keypoints i and j. The edge set E is represented by the adjacency matrix A, as expressed in Eq. (1).1\documentclass[12pt]{minimal} \usepackage{amsmath} \usepackage{wasysym} \usepackage{amsfonts} \usepackage{amssymb} \usepackage{amsbsy} \usepackage{mathrsfs} \usepackage{upgreek} \setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt} \begin{document}$$A_{i,j} = \left\{ {\begin{array}{*{20}c} {{1, }i = 1 \, or \, i = j} \\ {0, \, otherwise \, } \\ \end{array} } \right.\left( {i,j \in \left\{ {1,2,...,N} \right\}} \right)$$\end{document}
